lion dollars. However, I should verify if December 1961 data is available in the 1963 bulletin, as the fiscal year runs from July to June, meaning the November 1961 data would be part of fiscal 1962.\n\nExamining the 1963 page, I notice December 1961 data is present, showing total paper money at 31,336 million dollars. This allows me to compute the full calendar year 1961 change: 31,336 - 30,442 = 894 million dollars in paper money added during that year.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_41ff66f97d9845b8bd7fd6aa","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Find the year when treasury notes of 1890 were removed from U.S. federal government ledgers (1961)\n- [x] Find how much paper money was added in circulation that year (894 million)\n- [ ] Report answer in millions of nominal dollars to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
